When a page leaves full screen, Ladybird now asks for its window to be
maximized again if it was before. On macOS, Chromium and Firefox come
back zoomed as well, since neither asks for the normal state after
the transition, and both guard their own zoom calls with isZoomed
(Chromium’s NativeWidgetNSWindowBridge::SetZoomed(), Firefox’s
TransitionType::Zoom in nsCocoaWindow::ProcessTransitions()). On
Windows, both restore the maximized state explicitly: Chromium from
FullscreenHandler’s saved_window_info_, and Firefox from FrameState’s
mPreFullscreenSizeMode. Read from source (Chromium e6c8d7c15aeb2,
Firefox 41db707342fe), not run.
